{"key":"GorpEquationWindow","text":"## GorpEquationWindow\n\nThe **Gorp Equation Window** is a visual mathematical expression editor.\nBuild equations by combining nodes on an interactive canvas, then save the\nresult as a MathML-compatible Gorp algorithm.\n\n---\n\n@layout\nTitle Bar | 0.50, 0.04 | Right-click for Save to GitHub (persists as Gorp algorithm XML) and Undo/Redo options. Ctrl+Z to undo, Ctrl+Shift+Z to redo (up to 50 steps).\nEquation Canvas | 0.50, 0.50 | Visual expression builder. Click a grey slot to open the slot editor and choose Variable, Literal, Unary, Binary, Comparison, or Logical. Right-click a node to delete, wrap in negation/parentheses/sqrt, or use power-delete options. Double-click a variable or literal to rename/change its value.\n\n---\n\n### Building Expressions\n\n- **Click a slot** (grey placeholder) to open the slot editor\n- In the slot editor, choose a node type:\n  - **Variable** — a named input (e.g. `x`, `count`)\n  - **Literal** — a numeric constant (e.g. `42`, `3.14`)\n  - **Unary** — negation `–`, square root `√`, or parentheses `( )`\n  - **Binary** — `+`, `–`, `×`, `÷`, `^` (power)\n  - **Comparison** — `<`, `>`, `≤`, `≥`, `=`\n  - **Logical** — `AND`, `OR`, `NOT`\n- Each node that accepts operands shows sub-slots for its children\n\n---\n\n### Editing Nodes\n\n- **Click** a node to select it\n- **Right-click** a node for options:\n  - Delete node\n  - Wrap in negation / parentheses / square root\n  - For power nodes: *Delete Power, keep base* / *keep exponent* / *Delete Upwards chain*\n- **Double-click** a variable or literal to rename/change its value\n\n---\n\n### Undo / Redo\n\n- **Ctrl+Z** — undo last change\n- **Ctrl+Shift+Z** — redo\n- **Right-click the canvas background** — shows Undo / Redo options when available\n- History is kept up to **50 steps**\n\n---\n\n### Saving\n\nRight-click the title bar → **Save to GitHub** to persist the equation as\na Gorp algorithm XML file. Closing the window, or hiding the browser tab,\nsaves unsaved changes too, as long as the algorithm has a name.\n\n---\n\n### Video\n\nHelp/Videos/GorpEquationWindow.mp4\n\n### Status: Stable\n### Purpose: AIDesign\n\n---","screenshot":""}